	<div class="text-center">
		<h1>Kenjiro Shinozuka</h1>
		<figure>
			<img src="~/images/dakar/driver/Shinozuka/Shinozuka.jpg" />
		</figure>
		<p class="title">
			Kenjiro Shinozuka
		</p>
		<h2>
			(Japan - 20 November 1948)
		</h2>
		<p>
			The name Shinozuka is highly respected in Japanese motorsport circles. He began
			his career in 1968 and, in 1976, was the first Japanese driver to take the Kenyan Safari
			Rally to the finish. 15 years later he became the first Japanese winner
			of a round of the World Rally Championship, namely the Côte d'Ivoire - Bandama Rally in 1991.
			After his long years of collaboration with Mitsubishi, Shinozuka is one of the
			most talented and experienced drivers, as well as an excellent tactician.
		</p>
	</div>
